  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "For $\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}, \\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{GaCl}_{3}$ the increasing order of ionic character is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "JEwPH",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}     < \\mathrm{AlCl}_{3} < \\mathrm{GaCl}_{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8bwzv",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{GaCl}_{3}     < \\mathrm{AlCl}_{3} < \\mathrm{BCl}_{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Z6TJW",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}     < \\mathrm{GaCl}_{3} < \\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cK1D6",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{ACCl}_{3}     < \\mathrm{BCl}_{3} < \\mathrm{GaCl}_{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, ionic character is inversely proportional to polarising power of cation therefore correct order is\r\n$$\r\n\\mathrm{AICl}_{3}>\\mathrm{GaCl}_{3}>\\mathrm{BCl}_{3}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
